## 10. Conclusion

The operator's instinct to formalize a meta-project layer is strongly validated by converging research and industry practice. The layer is architecturally distinct from execution-layer agent orchestration and benefits from explicit definition. The recommended implementation is a **spec-anchored dual-loop architecture** with three persistent artifacts (constitution, living spec with frozen/mutable sections, progress ledger), a standardized questioning protocol for front-loading spec quality, and explicit review gates between execution cycles. This maps cleanly to the operator's existing `.agent/` scaffold and inter-agent handoff contract system, requiring primarily consolidation and formalization of patterns already in informal use.
